    "reviewer": "claude-code S339",
    "findings": [
      "S339 CANON-053 pass, final capture against candidate 523a93e04d63 after a full rebuild rotated the shell hash (receipts bind the candidate manifest, so any reseal invalidates them regardless of whether a pixel changed - D-S338.5). Home re-inspected in dark and light at 1366px: one status pill per hero tile, no amber second label, no clipped bare 'S' on narrow tiles. Root cause was the cover artwork rather than markup - build-game-covers.mjs rasterized the status word directly under the absolutely-positioned badge, and background-size:cover clipped it on narrow tiles; a Playwright DOM probe finding exactly one status node per tile is what ruled out markup and client-side injection and pointed at the asset (D-S339.6). The Sparked tier holds all five products the canonical feeds call SPARKED, no per-card badge remains anywhere in the tier grid, and the stray 'Sparked' meta chip is gone. KNOWN AND CARRIED, not a regression: the artwork still renders the genre eyebrow and title beneath the tile's own live kicker and name, on the board as [S339][UX/P3] to be decided as a design question with captures at both tile sizes rather than patched per breakpoint. Capture caveat: the full-page matrix catches the hero lede mid-reveal, so lede opacity in those frames is an animation artifact and not a contrast defect."
    ],
    "fixesApplied": [],
    "blockingDefectsOpen": 0,
    "limitation": null
  },
